+             * CPU-address page table and is PRE-BIASED, so the access idiom is
+             * Page[A >> 11][A] -- index with the FULL cpu address, not an
+             * offset into the page (same subtlety as VPage above). A NULL slot
+             * (no WRAM mapped there) reads back as 0. */
+            int i;
+            uint8_t *p0 = Page[0x6000 >> 11];
+            int contiguous = (p0 != NULL);
+            /* Prefer returning the LIVE pointer so the region is writable, not
+             * just readable -- retro_get_memory_data hands the host a pointer it
+             * may write through. Page[] is pre-biased, so the bytes for $6000
+             * start at p0 + 0x6000, and the four 2KB slots are contiguous only
